---
// Netlify serves this page for every unknown address (the English one for
// addresses under /en/, see netlify.toml). Before giving up it asks WordPress
// whether a post with that address exists: a post published a minute ago may
// simply not have been built yet.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ui, href } from '../lib/i18n.js';
import { API } from '../lib/wp.js';

const { lang } = Astro.props;
const t = ui[lang];
---

<Base lang={lang} path="/" title="404">
  <meta slot="head" name="robots" content="noindex" />
  <main id="inhalt" class="page">
    <div class="lost" id="lost">
      <p class="code">ERR_FOLIO_NOT_FOUND</p>
      <h1 id="lost-title">{t.notFoundLoading}</h1>
      <p id="lost-text" hidden>{t.notFoundText}</p>
      <a class="button" id="lost-link" href={href(lang, '/posts/')} hidden>{t.toBlog}</a>
    </div>
    <div class="leaf-grid" id="found" hidden>
      <aside class="side"><a class="back" href={href(lang, '/posts/')}>← {t.back}</a></aside>
      <article class="paper" id="found-article" lang="de">
        <h1 class="title" id="found-title"></h1>
        <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="prose" id="found-body"></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script is:inline define:vars={{ API, title: t.notFoundTitle, english: lang === 'en' }}>
    (async () => {
      const giveUp = () => {
        document.getElementById('lost-title').textContent = title;
        document.getElementById('lost-text').hidden = false;
        document.getElementById('lost-link').hidden = false;
      };
      const parts = location.pathname.split('/').filter(Boolean);
      const slug = parts[0] === 'en' ? parts[1] : parts[0];
      if (!slug || parts.length > (parts[0] === 'en' ? 2 : 1) || !/^[a-z0-9-]+$/i.test(slug)) return giveUp();
      try {
        const res = await fetch(`${API}wp/v2/posts?slug=${encodeURIComponent(slug)}&acf_format=standard&_fields=title,content,acf`);
        const posts = res.ok ? await res.json() : [];
        if (!posts.length) return giveUp();
        // Content comes from the site's own WordPress, the same source as every built page.
        const acf = posts[0].acf && !Array.isArray(posts[0].acf) ? posts[0].acf : {};
        const inEnglish = english && (acf.content_en || '').trim();
        if (inEnglish && acf.title_en) document.getElementById('found-title').textContent = acf.title_en;
        else document.getElementById('found-title').innerHTML = posts[0].title.rendered;
        document.getElementById('found-body').innerHTML = inEnglish ? acf.content_en : posts[0].content.rendered;
        if (inEnglish) document.getElementById('found-article').lang = 'en';
        document.title = document.getElementById('found-title').textContent + ' · Carlos Ha';
        document.getElementById('lost').hidden = true;
        document.getElementById('found').hidden = false;
      } catch (err) {
        giveUp();
      }
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
